  "signature": "_rank_functions(funcs_info: list[dict], classes: list[dict], signals: dict[str, set[str]]) -> list[dict]",
  "pre_condition": "funcs_info is a non-empty list of dicts. Each dict contains: 'name' (string, the function identifier), 'start' (int, function start line number), 'end' (int, function end line number), 'idents' (set of lowercase string identifiers appearing in the function), 'calls' (list of string names of functions called within the body), 'body_words' (set of lowercase string words from the function body text), and 'exc_types' (set of lowercase string exception-type names referenced in the body). classes is a list of dicts, each containing 'method_linenos' (list of int start line numbers of member methods). signals is a dict keyed by signal-category strings, each value a set of lowercase string tokens.",
  "post_condition": "Returns a list containing every dict from funcs_info, each augmented with a 'score' key holding a non-negative float. The list is sorted in descending order by score. The final score for each entry is the sum of three additive components: (1) a weighted multi-tier heuristic match between the entry's metadata and the signal token sets — with traceback-function-name signals weighted highest, followed by dotted-reference signals, then backtick-identifier matches in name and body, plain-identifier overlap in name, exception-type signals found in the entry's exception types, and body-word overlap with intent tokens scaled inversely by the square root of the function's body line count; (2) a one-hop call-graph enrichment where, for every function with a positive unenriched score, each function whose name appears in that function's 'calls' list receives a fixed fraction of the caller's unenriched score, and each function that lists that function's name in its own 'calls' list receives a smaller fixed fraction of the callee's unenriched score; and (3) when classes is non-empty, a class-scope enrichment where member functions of classes whose name and docstring tokens overlap with signal tokens receive a per-method additive bonus that is proportional to a class-level match score and capped at a fixed maximum value per method. Two entries with the same name and the same 'start' line number (signifying duplicate entries) are scored independently."
}
"}

{"filePath": "/home/fancy/Projects_Vault/FM-Agent/fm_agent/extracted_functions/src/scope-py/_rank_functions.py.info.json", "content": "{
  "callees": [
    {
      "name": "_base_score",
      "signature": "_base_score(name: str, idents: set[str], body_words: set[str], exc_types: set[str], body_lines: int, signals: dict[str, set[str]]) -> float",
      "pre_condition": "name is a non-empty string. idents is a set of lowercase identifier strings extracted from the function. body_words is a set of lowercase word strings from the function body. exc_types is a set of lowercase exception-type name strings. body_lines is a positive integer representing the number of source lines in the function body. signals is a dict of pre-parsed signal token sets keyed by signal category (including 'traceback_funcs', 'backtick_idents', 'dotted_refs', 'plain_idents', 'exception_types', 'all_words').",
      "post_condition": "Returns a non-negative float representing the weighted sum of signal match scores. The score incorporates: exact overlap of name with traceback-function signals, identifier overlap with backtick signals in the name and body, overlap with dotted-reference signals, name overlap with plain-identifier signals, exception-type signal tokens appearing in exc_types, word overlap between body_words and all-words signals scaled inversely by the square root of body_lines, and fuzzy substring matching between name and plain-identifier signals above a minimum character-length threshold. Each signal category carries a distinct weight."
    },
    {
      "name": "_score_class",
      "signature": "_score_class(cls: dict, signals: dict[str, set[str]]) -> float",
      "pre_condition": "cls is a dict containing the class metadata, including its name string and a docstring text. signals is a dict of pre-parsed signal token sets keyed by signal category.",
      "post_condition": "Returns a non-negative float representing the match score between the class and the intent signals. The score is the weighted sum of: per-token overlap between the class name tokens and the signal token sets, plus per-token overlap between the class docstring tokens and the signal token sets."
    }
  ]
}
"}

